# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project-specific additions (YourPeer chatbot)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
# Mutation testing (cosmic-ray + mutmut). cosmic-ray stores session
# state in SQLite files (cr.sqlite + per-module cr-*.sqlite files from
# `make mutation`). cosmic-ray.toml is regenerated by the Makefile on
# every run — the Makefile is the source of truth. mutmut patterns
# are preemptive (we use cosmic-ray) but would appear if anyone tries
# that tool.
cr.sqlite
cr-*.sqlite
cosmic-ray.toml
mutants/
.mutmut-cache
.mutmut-cache/
 
# Eval results. The admin panel's "Run Evals" button writes
# eval_report.json at the repo root — these files contain full
# scenario transcripts that should not be committed.
/eval_report.json
/eval_report*.json
/eval_results/
 
# Runtime data directories anchored to the repo root. These are
# generated or populated during local dev, not meant to be
# version-controlled. The leading `/` anchors to the repo root so
# these patterns don't accidentally block commits of
# backend/app/models/ (Pydantic schemas) or backend/app/rag/data/
# (the NYC boroughs GeoJSON) — both of which are real source code.
/data/
/pilot_data/
/models/
/sentence-transformers/
 
# Transcripts and session exports (if ever saved to disk locally)
/transcripts/
*transcript*
*session_data*
*conversation_log*